# 🚀 AIFS GPU Cluster Go-To-Market (GTM) Strategy

## 🎯 Objective
Position **AIFS (AI File System Accelerator)** as a **checkpoint acceleration layer** for GPU cluster providers that:
- reduces GPU idle time  
- improves training throughput  
- increases cluster monetization  

---

# 💥 Core Problem

GPU cloud providers face key challenges:

- **Checkpoint bottlenecks** → GPUs sit idle during writes  
- **Burst write storms** → shared storage gets overloaded  
- **Expensive storage scaling** → parallel FS / premium tiers required  
- **Lower utilization** → lost revenue per GPU  

👉 In large AI training jobs, **storage becomes the bottleneck—not GPUs**

---

# ✅ AIFS Value Proposition

## 1. Performance
- Absorbs checkpoint writes into **local NVMe (3–6 GB/s)**
- Asynchronous flush to backend storage  
- Eliminates write stalls in training loop  

## 2. GPU Efficiency
- Reduces idle GPU cycles during checkpointing  
- Improves **effective utilization by 5–20%**

## 3. Faster Training
- Shortens wall-clock training time  
- Increases cluster throughput (more jobs/week)

## 4. Cost Optimization
- Reduces need for premium storage tiers  
- Enables use of lower-cost backend storage  

